# mini-LMS decisions

Read `docs/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/CONTEXT.md`, and `docs/adr/` before changing scope.

- v1 is course pages: presentations, tests, and stored submissions. 3D chemistry labs, the pdb-viewer catalog, and offline `.labres` files are out of v1.
- Learners are adults. Names and email may be stored. Do not build the school pseudonym, PIN card, or teacher-key encryption scheme unless a later decision says so.
- A presentation is site pages. Do not ship the source PowerPoint or PDF to students and do not add a Download button. Do not claim screenshots are blocked.
- The teacher authors tests in a browser form: question text, a chosen number of options, LaTeX, basic formatting, and uploaded images. Hand-edited JSON is not the teacher's workflow.
- Published tests include which options are correct so the page can score on GitHub Pages. Do not mark the correct options for the student. After Check, show the score and which questions were right or wrong.
- A student types a name and no email for now. The stored name is whatever they typed. Do not add accounts or PIN cards for students in v1.
- v1 questions are choice questions only (one or many correct; text or image options) and are auto-scored. Numeric calculation items are post-v1.
- The teacher uploads a finished PowerPoint or PDF from a file dialog on the teacher pages. Students page through slides. Do not build a slide editor, do not offer the source file, and do not promise animations.
- Teacher pages (authoring, deck upload, submissions) require the teacher's name and password. The development login is stored only in the gitignored local file. Students have no password. A test or deck stays a draft until the teacher publishes it.
- Images in questions are uploads. Generate pictures in chat when asked, then the teacher inserts the file. Do not add an in-form image-generation button. A question may show one picture with its wording, and each option may have its own picture.
- Correct options stay unmarked on the test page. After Check, the student sees "Sent", the score, and which questions were right or wrong. Score in the browser from the published key so GitHub Pages can grade without a server. Retakes are a per-test switch, on by default. When the teacher server is running, each accepted submit is still a new attempt; the attempt number is per typed name + test.
- The teacher course list opens in sections: course, presentations, announcements, materials, each test, and each question. Announcements and method materials support bold, italic, links, alignment, and paragraphs. Each stays hidden until that section is published.
- The public site asks for the entry word before any course page. The word is hep2026 and is stored in the site script; it is a shared door code, not a private password. Remember it in the browser after a correct entry. Do not put that gate on the local teacher pages.
- Score is all-or-nothing per question, one point each. Past attempts keep the test version that was submitted.
- A student on another computer opens the GitHub Pages site. Publish sends slide images into the repository so the site can show them. Do not commit the PowerPoint, PDF, or `data/` drafts. Do not promise that a visible slide cannot be saved.
- The page background is white for students and the teacher. Keep the green buttons. Make card borders slightly thicker so blocks stay visible on white.
- Student test images, both the question picture and option pictures, scale down inside a box, keep their aspect ratio, and are not cropped. They sit left under the text. The teacher types the box height as a whole-number percent of the browser window when inserting that picture. Accept only 10 through 40. An empty value means 20. Reject a number outside that range and keep the previous value. Each question picture and each option picture has its own percent. Pictures already stored without a percent display at 20. Slides stay full width. Teacher image previews stay small.
- The grade book is one Google Sheet, appended by a Google Apps Script bound to that sheet. The public site calls the script after Check, including when the teacher computer is off. The script URL is in the site code; do not put the Google credential in the site or the repository. A person who reads the code can post a row under any name and score. Do not add a second store to prevent that. Append a row after each accepted attempt even when the teacher computer is off. Columns are row number, the typed name, the score as an integer, and date-time in Moscow time. Name the score column with the question count, for example "Результат (10)". A new sheet starts when the teacher publishes a test whose title or questions changed. A draft save, a retake-switch change, or publishing the same questions again keeps the current sheet. The old sheet and its rows stay. Create the sheet on the first accepted attempt. If the sheet name is taken, append the publication date. If the sheet write fails, the student still sees the score and that row is not stored anywhere else while the teacher computer is off. When retakes are off, the writer rejects a second row for the same name on that sheet. Share the sheet only with the teacher's Google account. Put one "Ведомость" link on the teacher page for the whole spreadsheet; do not repeat it inside each test, and do not show it to students. The teacher moves between tests by sheet tabs. Telegram and the full-answer archive are out of this work. Do not put Google credentials in the public site or the repository. Do not store the grade book as a file in this repository.
